==Trivia==
*Ana was the first hero, and support hero specifically, to be added to the roster following the launch of ''Overwatch 1''.
*Ana's story draws parallels with the story of Horus from Egyptian mythology. During an altercation with a former friend (in this case, Widowmaker), she lost her eye. Additionally, both her and Pharah possess an eye of Horus tattoo.
* Her voice actress is an Egyptian woman who was recorded from Cairo.<ref>2016-07-13, [http://me.ign.com/en/pc/121331/news/blizzard-hired-egyptian-actress-to-voice-ana-in-overwatch BLIZZARD HIRED EGYPTIAN ACTRESS TO VOICE ANA IN OVERWATCH]. ''IGN'', accessed on 2016-08-11</ref> The voice actress' name, Aysha Selim, was not revealed until September 29, 2016 in a reply on the official forums.<ref>2016-09-29, [http://us.battle.net/forums/en/overwatch/topic/20746644497?page=2#post-30 "We were extremely fortunate to work with a very talented Egyptian actress named Aysha Selim on the voice of Ana (who we recorded all the way from Cairo!)"] Michael Chu. ''Battle.net forums'', accessed on 2016-09-29</ref>
*Ana is the sixth playable ''Overwatch'' hero in ''[[Heroes of the Storm]]''.<ref>2017-09-15, [http://heroes.blizzplanet.com/blog/comments/ana-junkrat-volskaya-foundry-map-coming-nexus Blizzard Virtual Press Tour: Ana, Junkrat and Volskaya Foundry Map coming to the Nexus]. ''Blizzplanet'', accessed on 2017-09-17</ref>
*As of October 2023, Ana is the most played hero in the series.<ref>2023-10-07, [https://www.reddit.com/r/Overwatch/comments/1701c6m/whoever_didnt_go_outside_this_year_needs_to/ whoever didn't go outside this year needs to confess now]. ''Reddit'', accessed on 2023-10-12</ref>

===Misc. Character Information===
*In Cassidy/Baptiste interactions in ''Overwatch 2'', it is confirmed that Talon has a bounty on Ana's head, and that it is larger than the one on Cassidy's. Assuming that this is the same bounty [[Orisa]] mentions in the original game, the price on Ana is over $60 million.
*Ana has expressed interest in going to a number of vacation spots, including [[Lagos]], Crete, Malibu, and Fiji. She has visited Copacabana at least once.<ref name="AnaQuotesOW2"/>
*Ana's memories were used to create the [[A-7000 Wargod]].
*Night ops used to be her favorite type of mission.<ref name="LostGhosts"/>
*The [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caracal caracal] is Ana's favorite animal.<ref name="AnaQuotesOW2"/>
*Ana's Bastet mask is over 3000 years old.<ref name="AnaQuotesOW2"/>

===Development===
[[File:Ana Amari Concept.png|thumb|right|Concept art of Ana and her daughter, [[Fareeha Amari]]]]
Ana was the first hero added to the game after its launch. Blizzard began with the knowledge that they needed another healer, since [[Lucio]] and [[Mercy]] were showing up in every game. A concept was the Alchemist, a character who could drink from a decanter and then jump really high, or provide an extra-long heal over time. Meanwhile, the team were struggling to place the personality of Ana, which they'd conceived independently. Her backstory positioned her as a crack sniper, but the game already had [[Widowmaker]]. It was thus decided that the hero would be both a healer and a crack shot, using her rifle both offensively and defensively. The Alchemist concept was phased out within a few weeks.<ref>2016-08-11, [https://www.pcgamesn.com/overwatch/overwatch-ana-prototype Overwatch's Ana was nearly a potion-swigging alchemist]. ''PC Games'', accessed on 2017-07-11</ref> Influences for Ana's visual design were post-apocalyptic themes and imagery. The designers wanted to show her as someone who was rugged and resourceful, living on the edges of society. Her "Wasteland" skin is based entirely around this idea. Strap, pipe, and cannister designs in the skin were used to emphasize a character that was scrounging anything she could to survive.<ref>''[[The Art of Overwatch]]''</ref>

Prior to being revealed, it was widely speculated that Ana and [[Sombra]] were the same character, resulting from the photographs of her Shrike mask being misidentified as Sombra.<ref>2016-05-19, [http://www.eurogamer.net/articles/2016-05-19-community-believes-a-new-overwatch-hero-called-sombra-could-be-unveiled-on-monday Fans believe a new Overwatch hero called Sombra could be unveiled on Monday]. ''Eurogamer'', accessed on 2016-08-11</ref><ref>2016-07-06, [http://www.polygon.com/2016/7/6/12108222/overwatch-new-character-sombra-sniper-support Blizzard releases major hint about Overwatch's next character (update)]. ''Polygon'', accessed on 2016-08-11</ref><ref>2016-07-06, [http://kotaku.com/overwatch-is-still-hiding-clues-about-a-mysterious-char-1781137255 Overwatch Is Still Hiding Lots of Clues About A Mysterious Character]. ''Kotaku'', accessed on 2016-08-11</ref>

[[File:Ana Wasteland and Captain Amari skin concept arts.jpg|thumb|left|Ana Wasteland and Captain Amari skin concepts]]
Several PR assets on Blizzard's press center website for Ana are labeled "Shrike" instead of "Ana", suggesting that her placeholder name during development was Shrike.<ref>[http://blizzard.gamespress.com/Overwatch Overwatch Games Press], ''Blizzard Entertainment''. Accessed on 2016-08-11</ref> The name Shrike was used for one of her epic skins, in which she wears a mask previously seen in pre-release easter eggs.
Ana was teased on [[Temple of Anubis]], with an opened document picturing her wearing her Shrike mask.<ref>[https://abload.de/img/sombra_or_not6wog7.jpg Documents depicting Ana wearing her Shrike mask]. ''Temple of Anubis''.</ref> Her scope could be seen being worked on in a GameSpot video.<ref>2016-04-21, [https://youtube.com/watch?v=jq-HwvYjLLg?#t=00m09s ''The Story of Overwatch: The Fall of Titan'', 00:09] ''Youtube''. Accessed on 2016-07-10</ref> Also in the video was an early prototype with a modified Widowmaker model seen in the character selection screen, in the support section.<ref>2016-04-21, [https://youtube.com/watch?v=jq-HwvYjLLg?#t=15m25s ''The Story of Overwatch: The Fall of Titan'', 15:25] ''Youtube''. Accessed on 2016-07-10</ref>

Ana was added to the PTR on July 12, 2016.<ref>2016-07-12, [https://playoverwatch.com/en-us/blog/20178523#patchnotes OVERWATCH PTR NOW AVAILABLE - JULY 12, 2016] ''Playoverwatch'', accessed on 2016-11-06</ref> She was added to the live PC version of the game on July 19, 2016.<ref>2016-07-19, [http://us.battle.net/forums/en/overwatch/topic/20747185139#post-2 [PC] Overwatch Patch Notes – July 19, 2016] ''Battle.net forums'', accessed on 2016-11-06</ref>
